<p id="p2">&#160;</p>
<p class="Note" id="p2"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: For CimCore, MetrisMCA, K-Scan there are limited options for Y and Z ranges, because these localisers do not support more than 65fps, 54fps and 40fps scanning rates respectively.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">&#160;</p>
<p class="parameterstitle" style="background-color:Transparent;"><a name="Turbo" style="background-color:Transparent;">Turbo functionality</a></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">MM D has the unique functionality for quick change of the frame rate, which is called 'Turbo Button'. When activated KUBE optimises the scanning parameters to obtain maximum scan rate for the connected arm.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">When in pause mode user could quickly depress the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'B'</b></span> button (like double-click with the mouse) and KUBE will switch to fast scanning mode. This means frame rate of <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>80fps</b></span> for <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>FARO Platinum/Titanium,</i></span> <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>65fps</b></span> for <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>CimCore INFINITE</i></span> and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>54fps</b></span> for<span style="font-style:italic;"><i>MetrisMCA</i></span>. The localiser window will display 'Fast Scanning...' which indicates that KUBE will scan with maximum available speed for the current hardware. When depress <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'B'</b></span> button again KUBE switches to the previous scanning speed and the localiser window will display 'Scanning...'. This option can be enabled in Scan mode tab.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Every time the user switches from normal scanning mode to fast scanning mode and vice versa a sound is played to indicate that change.</p>
